   "subject": "How to plot a specific model with ggplot2?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"line-height:1.7;color:#000000;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial\"><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">I have some data which I want to stick to\nthe EXD.2() model. I fitted this model with drm() function that belong to drc\npackage. Is there a way to plot this model with ggplot2? Below is my data and\nthe script of model fitting:</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"> </font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">cl&lt;-data.frame (Area =c(521.5, 689.78,\n1284.71, 2018.8, 2560.46, 524.91, 989.05, 1646.32, 2239.65, 2972.96, 478.54,\n875.52, 1432.5, 2144.74, 2629.2, 676.5, 925.6, 1510.13, 2159.2, 2444.74,\n575.52, 1045.42, 1676.5, 2769.2),</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Retention =c(95.3, 87.18, 44.94, 26.36,\n18.12, 84.68, 37.24, 33.04, 23.46, 9.72, 97.92, 71.44, 44.52, 24.44, 15.26,\n84.36, 68.44, 43.44, 23.36, 15.44, 87.44, 52.56, 30.93333333, 13.25333333))</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Plot (Retention~Area,cl)</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Library (drc)</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">m1&lt;-drm(Retention~Area,data=cl,fct=EXD.2())\nThe formula is: y = d/exp(-x/e).</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">summary(m1)</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">plot(m1,log=&quot;&quot;)</font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"> </font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Besides, could Residual vs Fitted and Normal\nQ-Q plot be produced by ggplot2? Thanks for your help. </font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"> </font></span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Best regards,</font></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Pinglei Gao</span></p><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font></font></span></div><font face=\"宋体\" size=\"3\">\n\n</font></div><br><br><span title=\"neteasefooter\"><p> </p></span>"
    ]
   ]
